# The ring's two tile layers. The map is `Map0008.json`, and what makes it
# worth a map is there: it loops on both axes, so the hero, the two
# walkers and the camera go across its edges to the other side.
# `tests/test_wrap.py` says what is tested.
#
# Its edges are open on purpose, so that every seam lets one through, and
# four lanes are clear of anything: row 4, where the leftward walker goes;
# column 20, the upward one's; and row 10 and column 12, the hero's. The
# trees, bushes and flowers elsewhere are landmarks, so that a capture
# across a seam shows which side is which.

# 24x16, 384 tiles per layer
# The two tile layers, in reading order: one id per tile, 24 per line.
# These are the ids the binary stores; what turns them into pictures is
# the chipset. Edited by hand, the count has to stay the same.
